        "prob_desc_output_to": "standard output",
        "prob_desc_notes": "NoteIn the first example you were initially at San Francisco, then flew to Seattle, were there for two days and returned to San Francisco. You made one flight in each direction, so the answer is \"NO\".In the second example you just flew from Seattle to San Francisco, so the answer is \"YES\".In the third example you stayed the whole period in San Francisco, so the answer is \"NO\".In the fourth example if you replace 'S' with ones, and 'F' with zeros, you'll get the first few digits of \u03c0 in binary representation. Not very useful information though.",
